speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I rise on a point of order. I wonder if the minister would be prepared to answer the question at this point. I see the minister is nodding his head.
Is it not true that this bill allows the government to borrow $14 billion in fiscal 1982, to spend the whole $14 billion in fiscal 1982 and that the hang-over provision of $3 billion is not necessary? Indeed, on the face of the bill the government could borrow the whole $14 billion in fiscal 1982 as suggested by my colleague, the hon. member for York-Peel (Mr. Stevens).
[ Translation}
